            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0463" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.506 Manchuria/24: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-30T17:00:00-05:00">October 30, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>262. Your 517, October 27, noon. The Department concurs in the recommendation
                    contained in the last paragraph that at this time no action be taken.</p>
                <p>Please continue to keep the Department informed of developments, including the
                    attitude of other interested governments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
